WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.510
The Griffin has Arrived!

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.780
Ota! Hurry! He's about to...

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.810
What a terrible dream.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.580
Linus 1 to Linus Team: Status report.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.540
Linus 2: All green.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.630
Linus 3: All green.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.090
Captain! What was that?

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.050
Linus 3...
to your left!

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.730
The Linus team has been destroyed!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.700
HQ! HQ! Please respond!

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:34.040
We've lost contact with all teams!
We're being jammed.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.620
What's going on?

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.880
Is it the thing we fought on Oshima?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.590
Impossible!
That's why we moved to Ogasawara.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.220
This location is top secret!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.760
Who do we have left?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:52.600
At the last check-in,
only Raven team responded.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.420
Something's wrong.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.500
Should we pull back?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.050
No, hold on.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.430
What is that?

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.820
What?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.370
<i>Captain! Captain!</i>

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.370
He was only toying with us.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.090
Is the radio up yet?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.050
Yes, but we're still getting static.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.760
Contact HQ. They left a message.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:07:02.440
The Griffin has appeared.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.520
Whose bright idea was that?

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.400
It's just harmless fun.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:11.530
Chief, you can't let him
get away with this.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:18.410
Don't worry. It doesn't actually
give any clue to our identity.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.790
I still think he's getting carried away.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.630
We need to keep him under control.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:27.670
You're too intimidating, Kurosaki.
I'll talk to him.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:07:59.370
Good work.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.580
Piece of cake.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.330
Looks like you've mastered piloting.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.710
I want to do even more next time!

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:09.210
Did you see the doctor?

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.880
I'm tired of these
head-to-toe checkups!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:16.010
The more you use the Griffin,
the greater its effect on you.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.060
They need to check you each time.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:19.600
Bud,

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:23.690
you have to make sacrifices,
if you want to be the best.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.400
The Griffin looks unstoppable.

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.780
Its first performance was superb.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:39.620
It certainly got a taste of real combat.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.450
Was there any damage?

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:47.000
A little on the legs.
It's good to iron out the details early.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.130
Excuse me!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.340
Okay, prepare for shipment
and load it onto the carrier.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.610
We've accomplished
something incredible, but...

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.270
But?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:13.440
I wish we could publicly announce it.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:18.370
Maybe you'd rather show off
the Griffin laying asphalt.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:23.620
The world will come to realize
the Griffin's supremacy,

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.160
and then its value
will be astronomical!

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.250
But we can't sell it!
Not only is it incredibly expensive,

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:35.170
but it's radically different from
every standard Labor format.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.470
We could sell the basic theory.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:41.720
Yes. Shinohara could
use it in their AV system.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.020
You mean the system
used by the Ingram?

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:48.690
Exactly. So we DO
have potential buyers.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:53.940
I think their control software
is still better than ours.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.820
Their code is guarded as
tightly as a military secret.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.200
I'd like to capture a
working 98-AV Ingram.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.950
After all, that's why we
created the Griffin.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:10.250
Then Bud could leave the message,
"We're number 1."

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.340
Did you catch a cold?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.800
No, my nose just started itching.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.800
Maybe someone's talking about you.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.390
I wonder.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.730
A dream?

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:35.190
It was horrible. I could
never see my opponent clearly.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:39.990
Alphonse kept getting hit
until he was nearly destroyed.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:43.030
I called Ota for help.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:47.450
I bet that was pointless.
Dreams can be pretty irrational.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:49.500
It WAS pointless.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.960
Ota's machine was wrecked, wasn't it?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.290
How did you know?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.920
It sounds like a pretty realistic dream.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.090
I hope it never comes true!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.800
They say a dream right before
dawn always comes true.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.100
Stop it!

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.480
You take incredibly
good care of Alphonse,

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:14.480
so naturally you're afraid
of him being damaged in combat.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:18.190
And Ota ALWAYS gets
damaged before you do.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.860
So... your dream was
fragments of reality.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:25.780
I get it! As I get better
at piloting Alphonse,

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:30.370
I'm willing to take more risks.
Of course I'd worry about this.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.080
So what if it's a premonition?
I can handle it!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.550
What are those idiots laughing at?

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:40.510
Ota, dear...

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.300
Yes!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:47.560
Pointless griping isn't going to
finish those overdue reports.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.310
Right!

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.890
Uh...

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:51.980
What is it?

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:56.610
I'd prefer it if you didn't
call me "Ota dear."

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:57.940
Why not?

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.480
It's bad for morale.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.360
Pooh! You're too stodgy!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.160
But...

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.120
Now finish those reports,
Ota... dear.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.800
Ota!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.880
Come on!
Let's get in some practice!

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:27.970
I don't know what Kumagami said,
but don't take it out on me.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:28.930
Why not?

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.770
We just heard from
the Captain's office...

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:35.350
They may want to increase
the number of divisions.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.270
So?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.230
Don't you get it?

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:44.070
If there are more divisions,
they'll need new captains.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:49.700
And the most likely choices
are either Kumagami or Gomioka.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.790
She's really going to
be riding you, Ota.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:13.600
Police
Headquarters

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:13.600
What are you going to do?

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.600
What do you mean?

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:22.150
If we all get new Labors,
you'll lose the Ingrams.

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.900
Nothing's final yet.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.530
You know the Chief wants it.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:27.570
In that case,

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.240
do you want to discuss
our countermeasures?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.540
Right now?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.290
Sure, why not?

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:36.620
I'm meeting someone.
Maybe tomorrow.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:37.960
Oh.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.580
Well, see you later.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.250
Okay.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.550
Sorry to call you so suddenly.
I appreciate you coming to meet me.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.230
No, it's been far too long!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.610
You haven't changed a bit.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.820
How's your husband?

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:10.660
Fine.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.830
So you still haven't started a family.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.040
I hardly expected to hear
that from <i>you.</i>

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.420
What's so odd about it?

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.960
We'll have children eventually.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.050
How's work going?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:30.840
Terrible. We're forcing software to
make up for rotten hardware,

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:36.560
and every year Labors pull
farther ahead of our Pythons.

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:38.390
Say...

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.690
How many Labors are there
that approach real human movement?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.650
Close to human movement? Hard to say.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.280
How about your Ingrams?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:57.580
That's Division 2. There's also the
Shaft Europe Type 7 Brocken.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:02.630
After that, the Toyohata SRX-70.
That's about all.

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:04.130
Why, did something happen?

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.340
It's nothing.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.180
Oh, okay.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.100
You've changed, Shinobu.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:16.680
Yeah?

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:21.140
You were never this mellow in school.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.820
You're nicer this way.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.410
Well, thanks.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.130
Shinobu...

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.380
have you ever heard of the "Griffin?"

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.970
The Griffin? No.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:53.180
Oh. Well, it was great seeing you.
Let's do it again soon.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:14.160
...and once I did that,
a whole bunch of them came out!

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:18.660
The stronger the love,
the greater the heartbreak.

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.800
You can't expect ME to tell her!

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.510
I want you to gauge her reaction.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.470
We already know what it'll be!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:37.930
I just want to make sure.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.530
It's so hot today!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:16:59.580
Why are you so quiet?

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:01.830
- Well...
- Yeah?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.590
I'll be blunt! Look at this.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.880
What is it?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:16.180
Shinohara Industries newest product:
An economy Ingram.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:21.180
This is your father's latest project?

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:25.060
It sure looks like an economy model.
What about it?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:30.230
I think HQ wants to shift money from
our Ingrams to these models.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.400
Whaaaaat??!!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.820
Calm down! Calm down!

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.580
I won't accept this!

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.290
Uh oh.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.830
Don't you "Uh oh." me!
Alphonse is perfect!

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.750
Each day, I continue to improve!
So why are we changing now,

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:59.590
after working so long and hard to
create good movement data?

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:00.760
Listen, Noa...

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:09.940
Don't give me that look!
The Captain knew about this, but...

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:20.320
You're exactly right, Izumi.
I'm going to go tell the bosses.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.410
They haven't made a final decision yet.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.700
Oh, it isn't final yet?

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:28.330
That's what I've been
trying to tell you!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.210
But...

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.330
No buts!

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:34.460
Excuse us!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.550
Officer Shinohara?

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.010
Yes?

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.720
Have you ever heard of the Griffin?

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:42.970
Is it a Labor?

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.760
Probably.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.180
Never heard of it.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.390
Thank you.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.020
Excuse us!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.360
What's a Griffin?

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.110
I don't know. That's why I asked.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.200
Wait until you hear
the other side of it!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.790
Why should I listen to
an argument that has no merit?

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.540
No merit?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:09.370
Absolutely none!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:14.670
You know full well how capable
Alphonse... the other Ingrams are.

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:20.180
After all this work, why should we
switch to different machines?

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:23.050
Are they already talking about that?

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:23.890
It's just talk.

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:27.850
But at least they'll upgrade to
a newer Ingram, won't they?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.310
Our Ingrams are too expensive.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:35.190
Isn't it Division 1's turn
for an upgrade?

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:36.980
I think they want to standardize.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.940
But the new models are so cheap!

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:41.530
Are they as good as
our current Ingrams?

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:43.280
I don't think so.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.320
See?

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:49.790
Then what's the point?
Why are they pushing this junk?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:54.500
I'll bet it's because they
want to add new divisions.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.130
Quantity vs. Quality?

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.550
Yeah. They think
lots of cheap machines...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.050
will be better than
a few really good ones.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.560
Hey, it's not what I think! It's HQ!

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:12.020
I don't like it. This whole
idea of new divisions is bad!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:13.480
Why?

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.940
Ota's worried about the human angle.

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.570
So if we give up the Ingrams,

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:31.910
Officers Gomioka and Kumagami
will head divisions 3 and 4,

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:35.040
and every division will
receive the new Labors.

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:38.040
Captain, is this plan final?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.090
I think it's a bad idea to remove
our greatest tool, the Ingram.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:47.260
But HQ thinks it's more important
to unify Second Section.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.550
What's your opinion, Mr. Sakaki?

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:53.270
I think Captain Nagumo has
to approve this new Labor first.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:58.230
I'd love to upgrade, but
we can't sacrifice quality.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:03.650
You don't think the economy
model can hack it, do you?

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.700
Well, judging purely from
the spec-sheet...

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:13.330
They claim to run the Ingram's
software as-is, but I'm skeptical.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:17.580
You expect our software to run
differently on the new machine?

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:23.050
Exactly. But we won't know
for sure until we see it in action.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.760
And I know exactly
where we can see it.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:27.930
Oh?

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.850
The International Labor Show?

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.930
It's the biggest show of the year.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.770
If Shinohara Industries is
going to sell this thing,

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:42.900
then they'll have a working
model and demonstrations.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:49.870
Tokyo International Labor Show

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:59.040
Splendid, splendid.

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.880
The world's largest Labor show.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:04.460
Wouldn't this be the perfect
place to unveil the Griffin?

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.380
That's just a touch risky, isn't it?

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:10.390
Oh, but the benefits would
far outweigh the risks!

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.430
So, do you think
Division 2 will be here?

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:15.020
It's highly likely.

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:19.810
Why the gloomy face?
You should lighten up, Kurosaki!

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:46.170
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:49.890
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:56.140
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:05.650
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:08.570
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:13.160
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:17.830
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:20.670
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:24.840
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:31.340
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:36.600
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:39.140
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:39.140 --> 00:23:42.350
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:46.440
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:52.610
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:58.660
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:05.290
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.970
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:09.970
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:19.890
At the Tokyo International Labor Show
that kid Bud busts in,

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:21.560
takes control of the Griffin and
starts attacking every labor in sight!

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:25.730
Ota's and Asuma's labors are
getting completely trashed!

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:27.820
Is this exactly what Utsumi's
been planning all along?

00:24:27.820 --> 00:24:30.360
Is he going to get our Ingrams
after all? And on top of that...

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:32.360
I gave Asuma my movement
disc for Alphonse-

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:34.360
So I can't even start him up
until I get it back!

00:24:34.360 --> 00:24:38.410
